    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0194" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2776</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d202-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-21T17:00:00+03:31"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 24, 6.20
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>416. … The transport <hi rendition="#italic">Rhodesian</hi> arrived from Montreal
                    with 5,800 tons flour which being transferred to Russian craft for <pb
                        facs="0195" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/> shipment to interior points, where
                    flour exhausted. Please advise what vessels <hi rendition="#italic">en
                        route</hi> Archangel with supplies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
